A||||7||ThatRickGuy||ARGGGRAH!!! really bad shop rant||||8||
Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||06-13-2001||06:11 PM||||This has got to be my worst experience w/ a shop ever!! <P>If anyone was reading my thunking noise thread, this is just a continuace, but since it's no longer anything of a technical nature, I'm moving to general chat.<P>Setting: A while back I took my car to a shop that I've gotten really good work and customer service from before. The old manager had left, but I figured it was still a good place....wrong! The job was simple, lower ball joints, and poly bushings, I brought them the parts and even grease. They told me the parts would not be covered by any warenty but the labor would, no prob. They had to throw on a pair of KYB shocks as the old ones were dead and the top bolts were rusted solid. so, $500+ later, I was glad to have the job done.<P>skip to a few weeks back, I started hearing a thunking noise while breaking/low speed turning. I couldn't figure it out as almost everything up front was new poly. then a friend pointed out the 1/8th inch gap arround the bushings. thinking it may have been an instalation error, I took it back to the shop. they told me that since it was a 'performance part' it wasn't covered under any warenty, but that they should have noticed the 1/8th in gap when assembling it. the owner agreed that if I got him stock bushings, he would do it over again for $140. so we measured the bushings and I called up the fiero store to see if they were the wrong size. The cust service there told me there should be a metal housing arround the bushing, and that I shouldn't be able to measure them with out taking them out. (lesson in humility, stupid mistake on my part for not noticing) so I call up the shop (about 6 times in one day, trying to get a hold of the owner) to tell him the problem (the manager refuses to get involved) so he told me to find what I could for parts and he would look to, and they would get the cheapest part to replace the housing. so I look arround and call abit, and find out that the housings are pressed in to the a-arm, so easiest solution is get a new set of a-arms. find a junk yard 5 miles down the road, $55 ea, that's not too bad. so I call back and leave a msg for the owner. today I called again, the manager said he ordered new bushings from GM, that may, or maynot come with housings (I'm guessing not) and they would be in in 4 days!!! <P>so, come this afternoon, after trying to get ahold of the owner all day (no luck) I'm getting pissed because they want to wait 4 days for a part that most likely will not work, when they could have a correct part in 4 hours for $50 more. so after work I cruised over to talk to the owner, who was standing arround on the phone. after a few minutes he finally hung up and we talked for about 5 minutes. <P>I pointed out that the parts he ordered will mostlikely not work, and the a-arms were only a 5 mile drive away. I told him I'm getting out of the marines soon and I need the car in trip condition ASAP. He said he want's to take the cheapest option available, and he's willing to wait 4 days. I was okay with this, I figure I can get by for 2 more days then come back and get it fixed after vacation. So then I said 'I know you wanted $140 for this, but it is obviously a labor error, I don't think I should pay to get it fix' he babbled about performance parts, and I reiterated 'the part had nothing to do with the incorrect installment' then he flys off the handle, telling me to 'kindly get back in my car, and wait 4 days' and I was just trying to keep him from getting pissed off so I tryed to change the subject, he continued on, almost threatening me by saying something like 'you don't want to piss me off, I'll tell you to f*ck off in a heart beat...' at which point I got in my car and kindly left. <P>I figure I'll call him while I'm on vacation, and if he won't do it for free, I'll buy the a-arms myself and use the money I saved to get a 1/2 page add in the local paper explaining their poor service. I've already contacted my engine builder to tell her to stop suggesting his place, and have passed word to everyone else arround here. <P>so far I've cost him arround $3200 in business, I have some friends who had there vehicle repairs assest there and were planning on having them do the work.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Voytek||06-13-2001||06:32 PM||||Hmmm, That Rick Guy sure sound like a nice guy... I wouldn't have just gotten back in my car and left.  Depending of'course on the fellow's size.<BR>Anyway, I hear your frustrations.  I've been there before.<BR>You should post the shop's name on here so others in your area don't make the same mistake.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||06-13-2001||06:56 PM||||Yes, with poly bushings you have to re-use the outer shells from the old bushings. The GM ones will come with new outer shells. But... it doesn't take a rocket scientist to figure out what's going on just looking at the old and new parts. "Performance parts" is no excuse... a <B>good</B> mechanic would have figured out what was going on right away. Plus... there are instructions in with the bushings!!!<P>I would find someone else to fix it. If they were <B>stupid</B> enough to stick it back together without the outer sleeves on the bushings, I wouldn't let them near my car again, not even for free!!! If you can't do it yourself, take it somewhere else.<P>Oh... My guess is the poly bushings are getting chewed up pretty good. You will probably have to replace them again when you do find outer sleeves (housings).<P>||||reg||8
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||06-13-2001||07:08 PM||||The name of the shop is 'Quantico Service Station' it's on Hwy 1 about an 1/8th mile north of the marine corps base. <P>Thanks for the info on the bushings, I think I'll probrably just try to get the outter sleeve from him and do it myself. the polys aren't looking too bad, they are tight front to back, so the a-arm didn't chew them up, just left 2 scratch lines were the circles are. <P>As for dealing with the guy, I was extremely close to not just walking away. It's so annoying that this is happening now, if it had been earlier in the year, I'd actually have time to take some legal action. even if I don't get all my money back, atleast I could bring up a public record of his poor service.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Galen||06-13-2001||07:42 PM||||My experince is most shops on Hwy 1 arn't worth a crap, atleast down here in Rockingham. Went to one one time, to have my oil changed. Stupid people couldn't get the oil filter off, didn't know how to reach it. I admit its a 88 with a 87 engine, but still. I had to end up taking the filter off and putting it back on. The only reason my car has been back is to get inspected.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> my rant for this hour..<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">     <BR> <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>  -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
